This repository contains original code. It re-implements, without copying source files, the
EAGLE-3 draft architecture, training objective and checkpoint format described by:

  - EAGLE-3: Scaling up Inference Acceleration of Large Language Models via Training-Time Test
    (Li et al., 2025, arXiv:2503.01840).
  - speculators (https://github.com/vllm-project/speculators), Apache-2.0, release v0.9.0
    (commit 1c800f2b053bcd538fc11bf49ec843d4dfa81a95). Used as the reference for numerical
    parity tests (tests/parity_speculators.py imports it at run time; it is not vendored).

Target model: mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3 (Apache-2.0, Mistral AI). The released draft
checkpoint contains a copy of the target's token embedding and output-projection weights (the
draft keeps them frozen), redistributed under the target's Apache-2.0 license.

Training prompts (first user turn only; all responses were regenerated by the target model):
  - HuggingFaceH4/ultrachat_200k (MIT)
  - ise-uiuc/Magicoder-OSS-Instruct-75K (MIT)
  - openai/gsm8k (MIT)
See data/LICENSES.md for revisions and splits.
